{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Whom, etc.</b> If the prophet comes to rebuke them, they do not understand, for because of wine they are not in their right minds, like children." "<b>Report.</b> A noun." "<b>Weaned from milk.</b> It is construct state and inflected, like השכוני באהלים (Judges 8:11)." "<b>Removed.</b> That they removed them, like ויעתק משם (Genesis 12:8), and the word is a noun [formed] from the root."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:34.504798359Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}